  nodeTextLayers:
  - title: 'What is an Insulin crystal?



'
    basic: "Highly concentrated insulin solidifies into a crystal. \r\nThis crystal
      can reach a diameter of 150nm and contains ~100000 insulin monomers. Scientists
      don't yet know what the exact crystal structure is, or why it happens."
    intermediate: 
    advanced: "Insulin crystallization is possibly a result of insulin enrichment,
      zinc enrichment and acidification of the insulin vesicle. \nThis phenomenon
      is widely acknowledged, yet the definitive in cellulo crystal structure and
      its evolutionary advantage remain elusive."
